    overview: ["Cupping therapy is a traditional healing technique that uses suction cups to improve blood circulation, relieve muscle tension, and promote deep tissue healing. By creating negative pressure on the skin, it reduces inflammation, detoxifies the body, and accelerates recovery from pain and injuries. This natural therapy is widely used for pain management, sports rehabilitation, stress relief, and overall well-being, making it an effective alternative to medication-based treatments.", "At HealStride, we offer the best cupping therapy in Bhopal, ensuring a safe and professional experience. Our therapy helps treat muscle stiffness, joint pain, migraines, arthritis, chronic fatigue, and sports injuries, improving flexibility and mobility. Whether you are an athlete recovering from intense training or someone struggling with chronic pain, cupping therapy provides long-lasting relief and enhanced healing.", "Discover the power of holistic healing with cupping therapy. Book your session today at HealStride!"],
    benefits: ["Improves Blood Circulation", "Reduces Muscle Tension & Stiffness", "Enhances Detoxification & Recovery"],
    detailedBenefits: [{"title": "Improves Blood Circulation", "desc": "Cupping therapy increases blood flow to affected areas, delivering oxygen and nutrients to tissues. This process reduces inflammation, promotes healing, and helps relieve muscle and joint pain."}, {"title": "Reduces Muscle Tension & Stiffness", "desc": "By creating suction, cupping therapy loosens tight muscles, relieves deep-seated tension, and improves flexibility. It helps with chronic stiffness, muscle knots, and post-exercise soreness."}, {"title": "Enhances Detoxification & Recovery", "desc": "Cupping therapy stimulates the lymphatic system, helping to flush out toxins and reduce swelling. It accelerates tissue repair, supports faster recovery, and strengthens the body's healing response."}],
    conditionsTreated: ["Chronic Muscle Pain & Stiffness", "Arthritis & Joint Disorders", "Sports Injuries & Recovery", "Migraines, Stress & Fatigue"],
    detailedConditions: [{"title": "Chronic Muscle Pain & Stiffness", "desc": "Cupping therapy relieves muscle tightness, spasms, and chronic stiffness by increasing blood flow and reducing tension. It is highly effective for neck pain, back pain, and shoulder discomfort caused by stress, poor posture, or repetitive strain. By loosening deep muscle layers and breaking up adhesions, it restores flexibility, improves movement, and provides long-lasting relief from muscle pain."}, {"title": "Arthritis & Joint Disorders", "desc": "Cupping therapy helps manage osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, and bursitis by reducing joint inflammation, stiffness, and pain. The increased circulation promotes nutrient-rich blood flow to affected joints, supporting tissue repair and improving mobility. Regular sessions help ease discomfort, enhance flexibility, and provide a drug-free, natural approach to chronic joint pain management."}, {"title": "Sports Injuries & Recovery", "desc": "Athletes use cupping therapy to speed up recovery, reduce muscle soreness, and prevent injuries. It helps treat muscle strains, ligament sprains, and overuse injuries by improving circulation and relieving deep muscle tension. By promoting faster healing and reducing lactic acid buildup, cupping supports enhanced athletic performance, flexibility, and injury prevention, making it ideal for active individuals."}, {"title": "Migraines, Stress & Fatigue", "desc": "Cupping therapy is highly effective for relieving migraines, tension headaches, and stress-related pain. By reducing muscle tightness in the neck, shoulders, and upper back, it improves circulation and oxygen supply to the brain. This therapy also helps regulate the nervous system, promoting relaxation, reducing anxiety, and relieving physical and mental fatigue for overall well-being and stress relief."}],
    procedure: [{"step": "01", "title": "Initial Evaluation for Cupping Therapy", "desc": "Detailed physical and functional assessment to identify root causes and anatomical restrictions."}, {"step": "02", "title": "Customized Treatment Protocol", "desc": "Formulating a targeted plan combining active modalities and progressive therapy."}, {"step": "03", "title": "Therapeutic Cupping Therapy Session", "desc": "Gentle, clinical-grade application under direct supervision of university-certified specialists."}, {"step": "04", "title": "Post-Treatment Care & Guidance", "desc": "Postural advice, ergonomic modifications, and guided home exercises for lasting recovery."}],
    toolsUsed: ["Medical Grade Silicone Cups", "Vacuum Suction Cups", "Organic Lubricating Therapy Oil", "Disinfected Release Needles"],
    faqs: [{"question": "Is cupping therapy painful?", "answer": "Cupping therapy is generally not painful. You may feel a mild pulling or stretching sensation as the suction increases, but most people find it relaxing and soothing."}, {"question": "How long do the cupping marks last?", "answer": "Cupping marks typically last a few days to two weeks, depending on skin sensitivity and circulation. They are not bruises and fade naturally without causing pain."}, {"question": "Who should avoid cupping therapy?", "answer": "Cupping is not recommended for people with bleeding disorders, severe skin conditions, or during pregnancy unless approved by a healthcare professional."}, {"question": "How many sessions are needed for results?", "answer": "Many people feel relief after one session, but chronic conditions may require multiple sessions for long-term benefits. The frequency depends on the individual\\u2019s condition."}, {"question": "Can I exercise after cupping therapy?", "answer": "It\\u2019s best to avoid intense workouts for at least 24 hours after cupping. Gentle movement and staying hydrated help the body recover and enhance therapy benefits."}],
